# stack/icedrive/icedrive.pin — WHICH IceDrive binary this image ships.
#
# THIS PINS THE CLI, NOT THE APPIMAGE (changed 2026-08-27). The 118 MB
# `IcedriveMounted-*.AppImage` is the GUI client and is no longer shipped or
# wanted: the graphical layer it needed was removed from the image the same day.
# `IcedriveCLI` is a 9.8 MB native ELF that does the same job headlessly.
#
# THE BINARY IS NOT IN THIS REPO AND IS NOT FETCHED BY THE BUILD. It is supplied
# ONCE by the operator, verified against the SHA256 below, and cached. Every
# build after that is reproducible and needs no network and no vendor at all.
#
# WHY NOT FETCH IT AT BUILD TIME: icedrive.net is behind Cloudflare and answers
# 403 to anything that is not a browser. That applies to the CLI installer too —
# `https://icedrive.net/download/linux/cli/install.sh` returns 403 and a
# `<title>Just a moment...</title>` challenge page, so the one-liner the vendor
# and every forum post quotes,
#     curl -s https://icedrive.net/download/linux/cli/install.sh | bash
# PIPES AN HTML CHALLENGE PAGE INTO BASH. Do not use it. Measured 2026-08-26
# and re-confirmed 2026-08-27.
#
# WHY NOT COMMIT THE BINARY: ~10 MB of git history per version bump, forever,
# for a vendor artifact this project does not own. (Less painful than the
# AppImage's ~100 MB, but the same argument.)
#
# HOW TO SET OR BUMP THIS:
#   1. Download the Linux CLI from icedrive.net in a browser.
#   2. bash vmtest/export-icedrive.sh --print-hash --from ~/Downloads/IcedriveCLI-v3.62
#   3. Put the version and that hash below.
#   4. bash vmtest/export-icedrive.sh --out vmtest/.out/icedrive --from <file>
#      It verifies the hash, caches the file, and stages it into the payload.
#      Later builds reuse the cache; --from is only needed again when this
#      file changes.
#
# UNSET IS A VALID STATE: the ISO carries no IceDrive at all and firstboot says
# so. export-icedrive.sh reports it rather than failing.
#
# FORMAT: KEY=VALUE, one per line. `#` starts a comment. Blank lines ignored.

# The vendor's version string, for the record. Informational — nothing keys off
# it; the SHA256 is the identity.
VERSION=3.62

# The SHA256 of the CLI binary. THIS is what makes a build reproducible.
# Measured on the operator's downloaded copy, 2026-08-27.
SHA256=341eccb27046452bcfc63a081d605a933e583a3db4757e8c98647921d0cb68b3

# Optional. If the vendor ever serves a direct, non-Cloudflared URL, put it here
# and export-icedrive.sh will try it before asking for --from. Left empty
# because no such URL exists today (see the 403 note above).
URL=
